<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Lab Overview</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="~/Labs.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <h1>🛡️ Lab 1 Overview: Firewall Rule Audit & Attack Simulation</h1>
        </header>

        <section class="prerequisites">
            <h2>📌 Prerequisites</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Familiarity with basic firewall and routing concepts</li>
                <li>Understanding of IP addressing and network zones (LAN, WAN, DMZ)</li>
                <li>GNS3 installed and functional with pfSense, Kali Linux, and Windows images</li>
                <li>Basic experience using command-line tools (Nmap, hping3, sqlmap)</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="description">
            <h2>🔍 Lab Description</h2>
            <p>
                This lab focuses on auditing firewall rules and simulating real-world attacks to evaluate network defenses.
                You'll build a virtual network with multiple zones, configure pfSense rules, and use Kali Linux to simulate attacks.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>✅ Design a secure network with LAN, WAN, and DMZ zones using pfSense</li>
                <li>✅ Configure firewall rules to control access between zones</li>
                <li>✅ Simulate port scans, SQL injection, and ICMP flooding from a DMZ attacker</li>
                <li>✅ Audit firewall logs and refine security rules based on test results</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="objectives">
            <h2>🎯 Learning Objectives</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Understand firewall zone design and rule management using pfSense</li>
                <li>Simulate and detect common network attacks from untrusted zones</li>
                <li>Interpret firewall logs to identify suspicious traffic patterns</li>
                <li>Implement advanced rule improvements and intrusion prevention tools (Snort, pfBlockerNG)</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <div class="actions">
            <button class="launch-btn">
                <a href="~/GNS3/Lab" style="text-decoration: none; color: white;">🚀 Start Lab</a>
            </button>
        </div>

        <section class="setup">
            <a href="@Url.Action("LoadSetup", "Lab", new {labname = "ALab1"})" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                🛠️ Lab Setup: Firewall Audit & Attack Simulation in GNS3
            </a>
        </section>

        <section class="resources">
            <h2>📚 Supplementary Resources</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><a href="https://docs.netgate.com/pfsense/en/latest/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pfSense Documentation</a></li>
                <li><a href="https://nmap.org/book/man.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nmap Guide</a></li>
                <li><a href="https://sqlmap.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">sqlmap Documentation</a></li>
                <li><a href="https://linux.die.net/man/8/hping3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hping3 Manual</a></li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <div class="actions">
            <button class="launch-btn"><a href="~/home/levels" style="text-decoration: none; color: white;">Levels Selection</a></button>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
